{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01236",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.7,
      "end_seconds": 6.91,
      "duration_seconds": 6.21,
      "text": "I mean, you know, hello, doctor. May I come in?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.76,
      "end_seconds": 12.05,
      "duration_seconds": 4.29,
      "text": "Of course, leave it there. How can I help?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 13.97,
      "end_seconds": 22.02,
      "duration_seconds": 8.05,
      "text": "Yeah, it's a burn on my forearm. I don't know what's causing it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 23.16,
      "end_seconds": 26.47,
      "duration_seconds": 3.31,
      "text": "I'll just record a few vital signs"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 37.37,
      "end_seconds": 40.05,
      "duration_seconds": 2.68,
      "text": "Right, nearly done with the readings..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 55.02,
      "end_seconds": 62.76,
      "duration_seconds": 7.74,
      "text": "Okay: respiratory rate 18, saturation 97 percent, pulse is 83 beats a minute. And BP is 128 over 71."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 63.92,
      "end_seconds": 66.15,
      "duration_seconds": 2.23,
      "text": "Is that alright, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 67.2,
      "end_seconds": 73.12,
      "duration_seconds": 5.92,
      "text": "I'll explain what these mean in a moment. Did it come on recently?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 74.77,
      "end_seconds": 78.79,
      "duration_seconds": 4.02,
      "text": "It's been one week, I'm fairly sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 80.36,
      "end_seconds": 82.44,
      "duration_seconds": 2.08,
      "text": "Is it accompanied by anything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 84.5,
      "end_seconds": 91.91,
      "duration_seconds": 7.41,
      "text": "So, uh, when it starts I tend to get a blister as well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 93.6,
      "end_seconds": 99.68,
      "duration_seconds": 6.08,
      "text": "have you had a burn on your forearm before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 101.2,
      "end_seconds": 108.35,
      "duration_seconds": 7.15,
      "text": "mm, a bit, about six months ago it settled by itself back then"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 124.71,
      "end_seconds": 127.31,
      "duration_seconds": 2.6,
      "text": "How about numbness at the burn?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 129.22,
      "end_seconds": 134.21,
      "duration_seconds": 4.99,
      "text": "So, not at all, no numbness at the burn."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 136.13,
      "end_seconds": 141.2,
      "duration_seconds": 5.07,
      "text": "let me check a few things. Any burn to the face or fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 145.34,
      "end_seconds": 150.24,
      "duration_seconds": 4.9,
      "text": "erm, no, no burn to the face or fever"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 150.77,
      "end_seconds": 155.52,
      "duration_seconds": 4.75,
      "text": "understood any change in your bowel habit or your stomach generally?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 157.59,
      "end_seconds": 159.38,
      "duration_seconds": 1.79,
      "text": "Nothing unusual, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 162.73,
      "end_seconds": 165.62,
      "duration_seconds": 2.89,
      "text": "Any problems with your joints or muscles?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 166.68,
      "end_seconds": 168.83,
      "duration_seconds": 2.15,
      "text": "I move fine otherwise"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 170.5,
      "end_seconds": 173.34,
      "duration_seconds": 2.84,
      "text": "do you have any chronic illnesses?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 177.52,
      "end_seconds": 184.43,
      "duration_seconds": 6.91,
      "text": "I've had anxiety, yes. I've been putting this off for weeks"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 192.86,
      "end_seconds": 195.03,
      "duration_seconds": 2.17,
      "text": "let's run through your medicines"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 200.35,
      "end_seconds": 202.6,
      "duration_seconds": 2.25,
      "text": "Escitalopram, once a day"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 204.41,
      "end_seconds": 206.73,
      "duration_seconds": 2.32,
      "text": "Do you know the dose?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 207.98,
      "end_seconds": 212.97,
      "duration_seconds": 4.99,
      "text": "10 milligrams, I think that's what's on the box"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 218.26,
      "end_seconds": 223.16,
      "duration_seconds": 4.9,
      "text": "Tell me about your routine, work, habits, that sort of thing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 224.49,
      "end_seconds": 235.85,
      "duration_seconds": 11.36,
      "text": "I live with my elderly mother. I work in accounts at a hospital. I'm vegetarian and have been for years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 237.8,
      "end_seconds": 241.49,
      "duration_seconds": 3.69,
      "text": "Is there anything relevant on the family side?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 242.5,
      "end_seconds": 247.57,
      "duration_seconds": 5.07,
      "text": "Okay, you know, so so my brother has epilepsy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 249.81,
      "end_seconds": 253.87,
      "duration_seconds": 4.06,
      "text": "I'd like to check you over now, if that's alright"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 255.7,
      "end_seconds": 257.2,
      "duration_seconds": 1.5,
      "text": "Fine by me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 258.58,
      "end_seconds": 260.25,
      "duration_seconds": 1.67,
      "text": "Let me feel here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 278.44,
      "end_seconds": 285.52,
      "duration_seconds": 7.08,
      "text": "It's a small superficial burn with an intact blister, about the size of a palm."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 291.33,
      "end_seconds": 293.77,
      "duration_seconds": 2.44,
      "text": "That's all I needed to check."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 301.99,
      "end_seconds": 313.65,
      "duration_seconds": 11.66,
      "text": "Having listened and examined, this looks most like a minor superficial burn. The The reason I say that is that your story and my examination fit together."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 314.64,
      "end_seconds": 317.85,
      "duration_seconds": 3.21,
      "text": "Is there something to worry about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 319.94,
      "end_seconds": 348.74,
      "duration_seconds": 28.8,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like a minor superficial burn. I'd like you to take paracetamol, 1 gram, every six hours when needed, three days. You take it by mouth. That should help with burn pain. Cool it under running water for twenty minutes if it happens again, and leave the blister intact. Don't skip meals, and try to eat smaller portions more often through the day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 349.49,
      "end_seconds": 363.31,
      "duration_seconds": 13.82,
      "text": "come back or go to emergency straight away if the area becomes red and hot please come and see me in two days that's everything on my side anything you're unsure about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 365.0,
      "end_seconds": 366.74,
      "duration_seconds": 1.74,
      "text": "That's clear, thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 368.28,
      "end_seconds": 369.59,
      "duration_seconds": 1.31,
      "text": "take care now"
    }
  ]
}